#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063965 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064354 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d49af8-8aed-5434-bbf4-12c90c658fc0" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Positive Number to a Negative Number"}] :question/id #uuid "4d61f8ae-cf47-5aa7-96f8-770a232509ea" :question/math-academy-id "e-13380" :question/problem "What is the value of $-6 + 9?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $9$ to $-6,$ we start at $-6$ on a number line and move $9$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/f3/f3fc6c865056b9a177ab65d7a4477102c3e0d28035a14230bdf8c630c262e270.png)\n\nWe end up at $3.$ So, $-6+9=3.$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-6+9 = 9-6 = 3\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063966 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064355 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b20f6b97-6531-5ece-a1d0-4d25d4895dab" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Positive Decimal to a Negative Decimal"}] :question/id #uuid "a92db588-62a8-5a19-8420-a38d25dd9088" :question/math-academy-id "e-13381" :question/problem "What is $-3.5 + 6.5?$" :question/worked-solution "We can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-3.5 + 6.5 = 6.5 - 3.5 = 3\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063967 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064356 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "169a836e-5209-53a1-bda9-0542b044819d" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Positive Fraction to a Negative Fraction"}] :question/id #uuid "a287913a-827a-56fa-8bbf-5f716dff277e" :question/math-academy-id "e-13382" :question/problem "Find the value of $-\\dfrac{7}{6} + \\dfrac{5}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "We put both fractions over a common denominator of $6$ and then add the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{7}{6} + \\dfrac{5}{3} = -\\dfrac{7}{6} + \\dfrac{10}{6} = \\dfrac{-7+10}{6}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the numerator, we can use either Method 1 or Method 2, shown below.\n\n**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $10$ to $-7,$ we start at $-7$ on a number line and move $10$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/6f/6fc38c489951a4c0f26a5ff0ddc3da199da9ac71a2afc396701f8999921cb4a6.png)\n\nSo, $-7 + 10 = 3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{-7 + 10}{6} = \\dfrac{3}{6} = \\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers in the numerator, and we get\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{-7 + 10}{6} = \\dfrac{10 - 7}{6} = \\dfrac{3}{6} = \\dfrac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $-\\dfrac{7}{6} + \\dfrac{5}{3} = \\dfrac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064355 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b20f6b97-6531-5ece-a1d0-4d25d4895dab" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Positive Decimal to a Negative Decimal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fa1dfaf1-bfb2-5467-8046-aad5191102e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa1dfaf1-bfb2-5467-8046-aad5191102e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445402} :answer-field/id #uuid "063dade4-c614-5849-9dd5-3fd50b05fb88" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445404}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b19e586f-b5e5-54ad-9f34-9f32c29b74be" :question/math-academy-id "q-171019" :question/problem "$-5.1+7.8=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-5.1+7.8=7.8-5.1=2.7\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445415 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064355 