nk} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445409}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "456bbb28-9f6e-59b4-94a9-4565fc858899" :question/math-academy-id "q-186761" :question/problem "$-4+1.3=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-4+1.3=1.3-4=-2.7\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445410 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064356 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "169a836e-5209-53a1-bda9-0542b044819d" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Positive Fraction to a Negative Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6964b9d9-786b-5c01-9b32-664218330975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6964b9d9-786b-5c01-9b32-664218330975" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{15}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445395} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d674a5c-fdfd-5d98-b059-a94b119773c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445406}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "04148a8c-1c50-5c75-a5ce-265853c3b05d" :question/math-academy-id "q-186817" :question/problem "$-\\frac{7}{15}+\\frac{3}{5}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We put both fractions over a common denominator of $15$ and then add the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{7}{15}+\\frac{3}{5}=-\\frac{7}{15}+\\frac{9}{15}=\\frac{-7+9}{15}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the numerator, we can use either Method 1 or Method 2, shown below.\n\n**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $9$ to $-7,$ we start at $-7$ on a number line and move $9$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/f2/f2d170548e38956afa1354e7df74f645ea5101c3dde6665c110ada01ab7a96b8.png)\n\nSo, $-7+9=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-7+9}{15}=\\frac{2}{15}.\n$$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers in the numerator, and we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-7+9}{15}=\\frac{9-7}{15}=\\frac{2}{15}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $-\\frac{7}{15}+\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{2}{15}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064354 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d49af8-8aed-5434-bbf4-12c90c658fc0" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Positive Number to a Negative Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0f87dd3-c5a5-5a23-a0fa-dcdeaa29cc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061526} {:answer/id #uuid "e8c153af-0058-5ac0-8b30-02d3d4d035d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061527} {:answer/id #uuid "0adcf169-53c7-56ef-bcf1-00d9a9a1799b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061528} {:answer/id #uuid "53654dc8-6923-5845-9475-77c7ebc038ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061529} {:answer/id #uuid "5924dbfb-3d48-58ba-8f79-d6b75da6f83d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0adcf169-53c7-56ef-bcf1-00d9a9a1799b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061528} :answer-field/id #uuid "18e6b584-5e04-5bc0-bc9f-b8282822fd3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186061525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cb242b99-ab83-53d8-8934-74c871e7838d" :question/math-academy-id "q-2021" :question/problem "$-5+6=$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $6$ to $-5,$ we start at $-5$ on a number line and move $6$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/a3/a33a6894112c333711ee25f2bb79abd458448d5c0d4131ddbc53f4f828cc161e.png)\n\nWe end up at $1.$ So, $-5+6=1.$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-5+6=6-5=1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064354 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "09d49af8-8aed-5434-bbf4-12c90c658fc0" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Positive Number to a Negative Number"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "029931bb-b5f8-5fb0-9873-fecc74600828" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445390} {:answer/id #uuid "23598180-5131-56ac-a678-284f1be0f865" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445392} {:answer/id #uuid "39bdbb7d-1c2e-52f0-adb2-575085e56b8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445393} {:answer/id #uuid "84427d74-3ee1-560e-bc68-770067d24981" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445396} {:answer/id #uuid "f6a526c1-f065-5fe2-8d96-7ea86354ca6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84427d74-3ee1-560e-bc68-770067d24981" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445396} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a262c79-dfba-55a4-a56d-f3ec1cfd98f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445405}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d61e161d-c16f-54c4-b847-5ce2fd8181a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-2111" :question/problem "$-2+4=$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $4$ to $-2,$ we start at $-2$ on a number line and move $4$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/29/291bb445c414ae60c0093038554a780370b3e4d747e7e51a737aa15ffa7a6cf0.png)\n\nWe end up at $2.$ So, $-2+4=2.$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-2+4=4-2=2\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186445411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064356 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "169a836e-5209-53a1-bda9-0542b044819d" :knowledge-point/title "Adding a Positive Fraction to a Negative Fraction"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bb6d7c8-0f9b-5a72-997d-9319e4d9909f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445391} {:answer/id #uuid "d2da51ed-49ab-5a35-8936-978067b61077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445397} {:answer/id #uuid "ef3643e8-e01d-5c50-898f-0a065ba5fe4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445399} {:answer/id #uuid "f221eb0f-a3ec-559c-96de-9b221d2f6830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445400} {:answer/id #uuid "fe1d4d2c-65a3-5028-a3c4-6fec7489e8ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef3643e8-e01d-5c50-898f-0a065ba5fe4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445399} :answer-field/id #uuid "54f6bfc9-156f-56af-9a68-93e35ceaafd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445407}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2f37489a-3f1a-5d45-bf2c-50769e7aa76a" :question/math-academy-id "q-42771" :question/problem "$-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{5}{6}=$" :question/worked-solution "Since both fractions have a common denominator of $6$, we can combine them to form one fraction, which gives\n \n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{-1+5}{6}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the numerator, we can use either Method 1 or Method 2, shown below.\n\n**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $5$ to $-1,$ we start at $-1$ on a number line and move $5$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/63/632e4bcce5b619f9a5c4dfb2c414a33da0e9567b7b4d8b15adb439da1b3dd88d.png)\n\nSo, $-1+5=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-1+5}{6}=\\frac{4}{6}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers in the numerator, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-1+5}{6}=\\frac{5-1}{6}=\\frac{4}{6}=\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{2}{3}.$"}]}
